# Models
catboost_info/

# Data lives on the HuggingFace Hub, not in git.
#
# `data/*` rather than `data/`: a directory-level ignore short-circuits descent,
# so the negations below would never be reached.
#
# What is out: the GLiNER checkpoint (~1.1GB — GitHub hard-rejects blobs over
# 100MB, and every re-train would add a full copy to history permanently), the
# raw GeoNames dumps (309MB, refetchable with `make download`), the staging
# corpus `make etl` parses them into (intermediate, rebuilt in ~45s), and the
# compiled artifacts. `make hub-pull` brings back what serving needs;
# `make hub-pull-all` adds the training corpora.
#
# What stays: the small text records of *what* was built. ner_meta.json is the
# only place a checkpoint's splitter contract is written down, and the metrics
# files are the only source the published model cards are allowed to quote.
data/*
!data/ner_metrics.json
!data/rerank_metrics.json
!data/gliner-geosearch/
data/gliner-geosearch/*
!data/gliner-geosearch/ner_meta.json

